Every power of two has exactly one set bit.
 Eg:   1  = 0001
       2  = 0010
       4  = 0100
       8  = 1000

Now suppose we have 2 + 2 = 4, in binary
        0010
        0010
        ----
        0100     , a carry occurs. So equal powers combine into the next larger power.

So when can two subarray sums be equal?
2 = 1 + 1

16 = 8 + 8 
   = 8 + 4 + 4 
   = 8 + 4 + 2 + 2 
   = 8 + 4 + 2 + 1 + 1          

This happened because there are two equal powers. If every exponent is different, Eg : 8 + 2 + 1, its binary 
representation is 1011. There is no carry. So every subset has a unique binary representation.
Therefore two different subarrays cannot have the same sum.

